1
00:00:00,080 --> 00:00:04,830
Sunday. The first of November, 2015.
Ten thirty-three in the morning.

2
00:00:05,147 --> 00:00:09,441
In the city of Ningbo, the highway
police post a short notice online.

3
00:00:09,441 --> 00:00:10,872
Sudden traffic control.

4
00:00:11,180 --> 00:00:14,280
The entrances to the Hangzhou
Bay Bridge are closed.

5
00:00:14,580 --> 00:00:18,755
The bridge is thirty-five kilometres
long. It crosses open sea.

6
00:00:19,047 --> 00:00:22,697
And on the road towards it, there
is one car that does not know.

7
00:00:22,980 --> 00:00:27,774
The man inside left his grandmother's
hundredth birthday party a few minutes ago.

8
00:00:27,774 --> 00:00:30,555
He left in a hurry. He
is wearing a white coat.

9
00:00:30,847 --> 00:00:34,576
He controls more money than any
hedge fund manager in China.

10
00:00:34,576 --> 00:00:37,622
This year, the market lost
five trillion dollars.

11
00:00:37,913 --> 00:00:41,463
His best fund is up three
hundred and fifty-seven percent.

12
00:00:41,747 --> 00:00:44,922
For twenty-two years, he
has known everything first.

13
00:00:45,213 --> 00:00:46,613
Not today.

14
00:00:51,913 --> 00:00:55,438
His name is Xu Xiang. You
have probably never heard it.

15
00:00:55,747 --> 00:00:58,972
In China, they called him
Hedge Fund Brother Number One.

16
00:00:59,280 --> 00:01:01,455
He gave almost no interviews.

17
00:01:01,747 --> 00:01:06,247
He came to work in a tracksuit. He sat
at the back of his own trading floor.

18
00:01:06,547 --> 00:01:10,797
In meetings he watched two phones.
One for prices. One for news.

19
00:01:11,113 --> 00:01:12,963
He let everyone else talk.

20
00:01:13,280 --> 00:01:16,541
A friend put it like this.
"Xu Xiang is always trading.

21
00:01:16,541 --> 00:01:19,505
If he's not trading, he's
thinking about trading."

22
00:01:19,813 --> 00:01:24,725
His first fund went up three thousand two
hundred and seventy percent in five and a

23
00:01:24,725 --> 00:01:28,513
half years. Over the same years,
the Shanghai index rose eleven.

24
00:01:28,813 --> 00:01:32,188
Nobody could explain it.
Plenty of people had a theory.

25
00:01:32,480 --> 00:01:36,455
And in the summer of 2015,
somebody decided to find out.

26
00:01:37,747 --> 00:01:39,722
Go back to 1990.

27
00:01:40,013 --> 00:01:41,888
Shanghai opens a stock exchange.

28
00:01:41,888 --> 00:01:45,988
A whole country starts learning what
a share is, all at the same time.

29
00:01:46,280 --> 00:01:51,155
Xu Xiang is in his first year of high school,
in Ningbo, a port city down the coast.

30
00:01:51,447 --> 00:01:54,901
His father works in a factory.
His mother keeps the house.

31
00:01:54,901 --> 00:01:57,522
Nobody in the family
has ever owned a share.

32
00:01:57,813 --> 00:02:00,863
He starts trading anyway,
while he is still at school.

33
00:02:01,147 --> 00:02:03,572
There is no teacher. He reads books.

34
00:02:03,880 --> 00:02:08,605
He sits in on lectures. He copies whatever
he can find about how foreigners do it.

35
00:02:08,913 --> 00:02:14,263
Then comes the university entrance exam.
In China, that exam decides your life.

36
00:02:14,547 --> 00:02:16,097
He doesn't take it.

37
00:02:16,413 --> 00:02:21,613
Instead, he asks his parents for thirty
thousand yuan. About five thousand dollars.

38
00:02:21,913 --> 00:02:25,613
And he carries it to a trading
hall on South Liberation Road.

39
00:02:25,913 --> 00:02:30,538
Years later, he would say that
1993 was the year he was born.

40
00:02:31,847 --> 00:02:37,097
The hall belongs to Galaxy Securities.
Second floor, up a concrete staircase.

41
00:02:37,413 --> 00:02:40,388
The prices are written on
blackboards, in chalk.

42
00:02:40,680 --> 00:02:44,730
The rules change so often that nobody
is sure what they are this month.

43
00:02:45,047 --> 00:02:47,773
And he has picked a terrible moment.

44
00:02:47,773 --> 00:02:52,846
In 1992, the Shanghai index rose
a hundred and sixty-seven percent.

45
00:02:52,846 --> 00:02:58,147
Between April 1993 and the summer of
1994, it falls by three quarters.

46
00:02:58,447 --> 00:03:02,997
Most of the people in that hall are
finished. In China there is a word for them.

47
00:03:03,313 --> 00:03:06,513
Chives. You cut them. They
grow back. You cut them again.

48
00:03:06,813 --> 00:03:08,763
Xu Xiang does not get cut.

49
00:03:09,080 --> 00:03:14,155
He builds a style, and he never changes
it. Buy fast. Sell fast. Always go big.

50
00:03:14,447 --> 00:03:19,239
By 1995 he is nineteen, and people in
Ningbo are telling a story about him.

51
00:03:19,239 --> 00:03:21,347
Two Shanghai gangsters, they say,

52
00:03:21,347 --> 00:03:25,372
fell out over which of them would
get him as a personal trader.

53
00:03:25,680 --> 00:03:27,880
A triad boss had to settle it.

54
00:03:28,180 --> 00:03:32,055
Nobody has ever proved that
story. But people believed it.

55
00:03:32,347 --> 00:03:36,007
At nineteen, he was already someone
you could believe that about.

56
00:03:36,007 --> 00:03:37,922
Then the market did something that

57
00:03:39,213 --> 00:03:41,413
made his whole career possible.

58
00:03:41,713 --> 00:03:45,060
In December 1996, Chinese
shares get a ceiling.

59
00:03:45,060 --> 00:03:50,188
A stock can rise ten percent in a day.
Then it stops. That is the limit.

60
00:03:50,480 --> 00:03:54,780
The rule is there to calm things down.
Now think about what it really does.

61
00:03:55,080 --> 00:03:58,751
A stock that hits the ceiling
still has buyers. They wanted in.

62
00:03:58,751 --> 00:04:02,130
They couldn't get in. So tomorrow
morning, they try again.

63
00:04:02,447 --> 00:04:06,547
The limit does not stop a rush.
It makes the rush wait in line.

64
00:04:06,847 --> 00:04:11,197
Xu and a handful of traders at Galaxy
work out how to start that line.

65
00:04:11,480 --> 00:04:14,105
Pick a cheap stock that
nobody is watching.

66
00:04:14,413 --> 00:04:17,638
Hit it with one enormous
buy order, out of nowhere.

67
00:04:17,947 --> 00:04:21,272
Other traders see the size
and pile in. Limit up.

68
00:04:21,580 --> 00:04:25,330
Next morning, the buyers who missed
out push it to the limit again.

69
00:04:25,647 --> 00:04:29,547
A few days later, sell everything
to the people still arriving.

70
00:04:29,847 --> 00:04:32,847
Then the price falls.
But you are already gone.

71
00:04:33,147 --> 00:04:36,397
The press gives them a name.
The Limit-Up Death Squad.

72
00:04:36,713 --> 00:04:39,888
Xu Xiang, in his early
twenties, is the captain.

73
00:04:40,180 --> 00:04:41,983
Soon they barely need the trick.

74
00:04:41,983 --> 00:04:46,040
Traders across the country watch which
stocks the Ningbo hall is buying,

75
00:04:46,040 --> 00:04:47,280
and buy the same ones.

76
00:04:47,580 --> 00:04:49,805
Their order has become the news.

77
00:04:50,113 --> 00:04:53,713
The others buy sports cars and
park them outside the hall.

78
00:04:54,013 --> 00:04:56,413
Xu doesn't. He buys more stock.

79
00:04:56,713 --> 00:05:01,538
There are books about them. Travelling
seminars. Copycat squads in other cities.

80
00:05:01,847 --> 00:05:07,372
And in 2003, a newspaper asks the
obvious question. Is any of this allowed?

81
00:05:07,680 --> 00:05:10,930
The regulator sends an
investigator to Ningbo.

82
00:05:11,247 --> 00:05:16,497
He calls in the big local traders for what
is described as an informal discussion.

83
00:05:16,813 --> 00:05:18,663
The Death Squad vanishes.

84
00:05:18,980 --> 00:05:20,405
For one week.

85
00:05:20,713 --> 00:05:25,713
Then the investigator announces that he has
found no wrongdoing. And they come back.

86
00:05:26,013 --> 00:05:28,613
Remember that week. It matters later.

87
00:05:28,913 --> 00:05:33,863
By 2005, the boy with thirty thousand
yuan has hundreds of millions.

88
00:05:35,180 --> 00:05:39,730
Ningbo is now too small. He moves to
Shanghai, and his timing is perfect.

89
00:05:40,047 --> 00:05:40,928
That same year,

90
00:05:40,928 --> 00:05:45,683
a change in the law lets private funds
step out of the shadows and operate in the

91
00:05:45,683 --> 00:05:47,797
open. They call them sunshine funds.

92
00:05:48,113 --> 00:05:51,863
In December 2009, he
registers his own firm.

93
00:05:52,180 --> 00:05:54,716
He calls it Zexi. Ze, from Mao Zedong.

94
00:05:54,716 --> 00:05:59,055
Xi, from Kangxi, the longest-reigning
emperor in Chinese history.

95
00:05:59,347 --> 00:06:01,097
Modest, he was not.

96
00:06:01,380 --> 00:06:05,565
In March 2010 he opens his first
fund with one billion yuan.

97
00:06:05,565 --> 00:06:08,355
It has fewer than two hundred investors.

98
00:06:08,647 --> 00:06:13,172
Under the rules, that means he never has
to say who they are. Remember that, too.

99
00:06:13,480 --> 00:06:16,630
He is at his desk at eight
forty-five every morning.

100
00:06:16,913 --> 00:06:19,788
He is often still there
at two the next morning.

101
00:06:20,080 --> 00:06:24,512
His own researchers only find out whether
he took their advice at the end of the

102
00:06:24,512 --> 00:06:26,230
year, when the results come in.

103
00:06:26,547 --> 00:06:30,847
Friends say he has no hobbies. There
is the market. That is all there is.

104
00:06:31,147 --> 00:06:35,496
The method has grown up with him. He
no longer just hits a stock and runs.

105
00:06:35,496 --> 00:06:37,847
He buys a real stake in a small company.

106
00:06:38,147 --> 00:06:40,272
He gets allies onto the board.

107
00:06:40,580 --> 00:06:45,655
The company pays out cash. He uses the
cash to buy more, and sells into the rise.

108
00:06:45,947 --> 00:06:50,797
Between 2010 and 2014 he does
this with forty-five companies.

109
00:06:51,080 --> 00:06:55,930
His own parents sit as executives and
shareholders across the web of firms.

110
00:06:56,213 --> 00:06:57,944
And the results are absurd.

111
00:06:57,944 --> 00:07:02,238
One fund returns five hundred and
thirty-six percent in four years.

112
00:07:02,547 --> 00:07:07,026
By 2015 he is the hundred and
eighty-eighth richest person in China,

113
00:07:07,026 --> 00:07:09,397
worth two point two billion dollars.

114
00:07:09,680 --> 00:07:13,109
So who were the two hundred?
It was said, and never proven,

115
00:07:13,109 --> 00:07:16,655
that some of them were the
children of very senior officials.

116
00:07:16,947 --> 00:07:21,581
A man who had worked in the industry told
a reporter that when a powerful client

117
00:07:21,581 --> 00:07:24,072
hands you money, it is
difficult to say no.

118
00:07:24,380 --> 00:07:27,605
In November 2014, Xu opens
an office in Beijing.

119
00:07:27,605 --> 00:07:32,980
It is less than half a mile from the
headquarters of the stock market regulator.

120
00:07:33,280 --> 00:07:37,428
His colleagues later said that was the
start of a year spent trying to protect

121
00:07:37,428 --> 00:07:39,555
himself. He could feel something coming.

122
00:07:39,847 --> 00:07:42,647
He was right. Then the
market did something that

123
00:07:43,947 --> 00:07:46,347
made his whole career impossible.

124
00:07:46,647 --> 00:07:51,897
Friday, the twelfth of June, 2015. The
Chinese market peaks. Then it falls.

125
00:07:52,213 --> 00:07:55,238
In three weeks, a third
of its value is gone.

126
00:07:55,547 --> 00:07:59,711
Remember who is in this market. Two
hundred million ordinary people.

127
00:07:59,711 --> 00:08:02,772
They make about eighty-five
percent of the trades.

128
00:08:03,080 --> 00:08:05,130
Chives, as far as you can see.

129
00:08:05,413 --> 00:08:10,350
The government throws everything at it.
Big shareholders are banned from selling.

130
00:08:10,350 --> 00:08:13,763
New listings are frozen. State
firms are ordered to buy.

131
00:08:14,080 --> 00:08:18,705
They call it the national team, and it
has up to three trillion yuan behind it.

132
00:08:19,013 --> 00:08:20,638
It does not hold.

133
00:08:20,947 --> 00:08:23,772
The twenty-seventh of
July. Another plunge.

134
00:08:24,080 --> 00:08:25,716
The twenty-fourth of August.

135
00:08:25,716 --> 00:08:29,805
Shanghai falls eight and a half
percent, its worst day in eight years.

136
00:08:30,113 --> 00:08:33,568
In New York, the Dow drops a
thousand points at the open.

137
00:08:33,568 --> 00:08:36,113
The state newspaper calls it Black Monday.

138
00:08:36,413 --> 00:08:39,238
Five trillion dollars, gone in ten weeks.

139
00:08:39,547 --> 00:08:40,922
And Zexi?

140
00:08:41,213 --> 00:08:45,623
In the worst three weeks of the crash,
all five of his public funds go up.

141
00:08:45,623 --> 00:08:47,888
Every one, by at least twenty percent.

142
00:08:48,180 --> 00:08:52,367
His best fund is up three hundred
and fifty-seven percent for the year.

143
00:08:52,367 --> 00:08:55,905
First place, out of one thousand
six hundred and forty-nine.

144
00:08:56,213 --> 00:09:00,013
His money seemed to step out of
the market just before each fall.

145
00:09:00,313 --> 00:09:02,963
In a normal year, that makes you a genius.

146
00:09:03,247 --> 00:09:06,672
In a year when the state itself
lost, what does it make you?

147
00:09:06,980 --> 00:09:09,738
Meanwhile, in Beijing,
people need an answer.

148
00:09:09,738 --> 00:09:14,826
The Party's own inspectors have begun going
through the stock regulator from top to

149
00:09:14,826 --> 00:09:15,626
bottom.

150
00:09:15,547 --> 00:09:18,123
Brokerage executives are being arrested.

151
00:09:18,123 --> 00:09:21,022
Everyone in finance is
asking the same thing.

152
00:09:21,313 --> 00:09:22,838
Who is next?

153
00:09:23,147 --> 00:09:27,855
In September, an anonymous post goes
viral. It claims that during the rescue,

154
00:09:27,855 --> 00:09:32,868
Zexi worked with a state-owned brokerage
to point the government's own buying at a

155
00:09:32,868 --> 00:09:34,397
stock Zexi wanted lifted.

156
00:09:34,713 --> 00:09:37,813
Zexi denied it. No court ever ruled on it.

157
00:09:38,113 --> 00:09:43,088
But the regulator is now looking. And Xu
Xiang is told he may not leave the country.

158
00:09:43,380 --> 00:09:46,855
Nine days later, his
grandmother turns one hundred.

159
00:10:08,147 --> 00:10:09,175
The party is small.

160
00:10:09,175 --> 00:10:12,747
His grandmother still lives in the
neighbourhood where he grew up.

161
00:10:13,047 --> 00:10:17,868
Shortly before ten thirty, according to
people who knew him, a warning reaches him.

162
00:10:17,868 --> 00:10:18,797
They are coming.

163
00:10:19,113 --> 00:10:20,713
He leaves at once.

164
00:10:21,013 --> 00:10:24,713
He drives north, towards Shanghai.
Past the concrete blocks.

165
00:10:25,013 --> 00:10:27,563
Over the river that cuts Ningbo in half.

166
00:10:27,847 --> 00:10:29,497
Out along the bay.

167
00:10:29,813 --> 00:10:32,513
The fast road to Shanghai has one bridge.

168
00:10:32,813 --> 00:10:37,083
For twenty-two years, his whole edge
had been knowing before everyone else.

169
00:10:37,083 --> 00:10:38,563
This morning he knew, too.

170
00:10:38,880 --> 00:10:41,630
A few minutes late. And
not about the bridge.

171
00:10:41,947 --> 00:10:43,522
They stop him there.

172
00:10:47,813 --> 00:10:52,488
That evening, a photograph appears
online. White coat. Rimless glasses.

173
00:10:52,780 --> 00:10:56,466
Someone's hand is pulling back his
sleeve, and you can see the cuff.

174
00:10:56,466 --> 00:10:58,580
He is looking straight into the camera.

175
00:10:58,880 --> 00:11:03,209
The internet does what it does. The coat,
people said, looked like a doctor's.

176
00:11:03,209 --> 00:11:06,705
Had he been arrested for practising
medicine without a licence?

177
00:11:07,013 --> 00:11:11,613
Two hundred million people had just been
cut. Now they had someone to look at.

178
00:11:12,913 --> 00:11:17,582
Then, nothing. When reporters reach
Zexi's offices in Shanghai and Beijing,

179
00:11:17,582 --> 00:11:19,388
the doors are already sealed.

180
00:11:19,680 --> 00:11:23,955
There is a word for what has happened
to him. Shilian. Lost contact.

181
00:11:24,247 --> 00:11:28,747
The firm does not survive it. As
one profile put it: Xu was Zexi.

182
00:11:29,047 --> 00:11:32,772
Thirteen months later, he appears
in a courtroom in Qingdao.

183
00:11:33,080 --> 00:11:34,855
And he pleads guilty.

184
00:11:35,147 --> 00:11:38,122
Now we get the answer.
How did he always know?

185
00:11:38,413 --> 00:11:40,999
From 2010 to 2015, the court found,

186
00:11:40,999 --> 00:11:45,063
Xu worked with executives at
thirteen listed companies.

187
00:11:45,380 --> 00:11:47,530
The company would put out good news.

188
00:11:47,813 --> 00:11:50,763
Xu would buy heavily, and
the price would climb.

189
00:11:51,080 --> 00:11:54,030
Ordinary investors would
see it and rush in.

190
00:11:54,347 --> 00:11:57,347
Then Xu and the executives
would sell to them.

191
00:11:57,647 --> 00:12:00,947
He knew first because he had
arranged what there was to know.

192
00:12:01,247 --> 00:12:05,395
Look at it again. It is the same trick
as the chalk hall. Start the line.

193
00:12:05,395 --> 00:12:07,497
Sell to the people at the back of it.

194
00:12:07,813 --> 00:12:11,113
The only thing that changed
in twenty years was the size.

195
00:12:11,413 --> 00:12:16,613
On the twenty-third of January 2017,
the sentence. Five and a half years.

196
00:12:16,913 --> 00:12:21,816
And a fine reported at eleven billion
yuan. One point six billion dollars.

197
00:12:21,816 --> 00:12:26,388
The largest ever handed to one person
for a financial crime in China.

198
00:12:26,680 --> 00:12:28,280
He does not appeal.

199
00:12:29,580 --> 00:12:32,505
So here is the question
this story leaves you with.

200
00:12:32,813 --> 00:12:37,988
In 2003, an investigator looked at the
Death Squad and found nothing wrong.

201
00:12:38,280 --> 00:12:43,580
In 2017, a court looked at the grown-up
version and sent its captain to prison.

202
00:12:43,880 --> 00:12:46,214
Was he a criminal who finally got caught?

203
00:12:46,214 --> 00:12:49,118
Or one player in a game
that everybody was playing,

204
00:12:49,118 --> 00:12:51,680
picked out because the
country needed a face?

205
00:12:51,980 --> 00:12:56,510
One fund manager said that many others
could have been detained for exactly the

206
00:12:56,510 --> 00:12:57,310
same reasons.

207
00:12:57,547 --> 00:13:01,847
The court's answer is simpler. He
broke the law. He said so himself.

208
00:13:02,147 --> 00:13:04,072
Both of those can be true.

209
00:13:04,380 --> 00:13:06,347
It cost him more than money.

210
00:13:06,347 --> 00:13:11,055
In March 2019, with Xu still in
prison, his wife filed for divorce.

211
00:13:11,347 --> 00:13:15,772
They had met in 1998, when he was
still the kid from the chalk hall.

212
00:13:16,080 --> 00:13:19,355
Around twenty billion yuan
of assets sat frozen.

213
00:13:19,647 --> 00:13:22,647
And the industry he had
ruled banned him from it.

214
00:13:23,947 --> 00:13:26,322
His gift was never picking stocks.

215
00:13:26,613 --> 00:13:31,238
It was knowing first. He built a life on
it, and for twenty-two years it worked.

216
00:13:31,547 --> 00:13:35,282
But a man who lives by knowing
first has exactly one weakness.

217
00:13:35,282 --> 00:13:37,872
The day somebody else
knows before he does.

218
00:13:39,180 --> 00:13:44,630
On the ninth of July 2021, Xu Xiang
walked out of prison. He was forty-four.

219
00:13:44,947 --> 00:13:48,447
The fine, by the last reports,
had still not been paid.

220
00:13:48,747 --> 00:13:53,171
A fund manager in Beijing once summed
up the whole business in one sentence.

221
00:13:53,171 --> 00:13:56,547
"In China, the losing side
doesn't get to sleep at night."

222
00:13:56,847 --> 00:14:00,872
As for the bridge. It reopened after
a little more than half an hour.

223
00:14:01,180 --> 00:14:02,930
The traffic moved on.

